User Story
As a Dynamics 365 Opportunity user,
I want file attachments added through Timeline Notes on Opportunity records to be automatically copied into the Opportunity’s SharePoint document folder,
so that the files remain available on the Note in Dynamics, accessible to users who do not have Dynamics 365 access, and visible in the Opportunity Documents tab.

Description
Currently, files added through the Opportunity Documents tab are stored in SharePoint and are accessible through SharePoint permissions. However, files attached through Timeline Notes remain stored only as Note attachments in Dynamics 365 and are not automatically available in the Opportunity’s SharePoint document folder or Documents tab.

A Power Automate solution is needed to detect Note attachments created on Opportunity records and copy only the attachment file into the same SharePoint folder used by the Opportunity Documents tab.

If the Opportunity already has a SharePoint document location, the file should be copied there. If the Opportunity does not yet have a SharePoint document location or folder, the automation should create the missing Opportunity folder in the same standard SharePoint directory structure used for Opportunity documents, create the related SharePoint Document Location record in Dataverse, and then upload the file there.

The original attachment must remain on the Note in Dynamics. Note text must not be copied.

Business Value
This will:

make Opportunity files attached from Timeline Notes accessible to non-Dynamics users through SharePoint

preserve current user behavior in Dynamics

centralize Opportunity documents in SharePoint

ensure files attached through Notes are visible in the Opportunity Documents tab just like files uploaded directly through Documents

Acceptance Criteria

Process only Opportunity Note attachments
Given a Note is created in Dynamics 365
When the Note is regarding an Opportunity and contains a file attachment
Then the automation processes the Note
And if the Note is not regarding an Opportunity or has no attachment, it is ignored

Copy file to existing Opportunity SharePoint folder
Given an Opportunity already has a valid SharePoint document location
When a user adds a Timeline Note with an attachment to that Opportunity
Then the file attachment is copied into the existing Opportunity SharePoint folder
And the original Note attachment remains in Dynamics
And the file becomes visible in the Opportunity Documents tab

Create missing folder and document location when needed
Given an Opportunity does not yet have a SharePoint document location or folder
When a user adds a Timeline Note with an attachment to that Opportunity
Then the automation creates the missing Opportunity SharePoint folder in the standard Opportunity SharePoint structure
And creates the related SharePoint Document Location record in Dataverse
And uploads the attachment into that folder
And the file becomes visible in the Opportunity Documents tab

Do not copy note text
Given a Timeline Note contains both note text and a file attachment
When the automation runs
Then only the file attachment is copied to SharePoint
And the note text is not copied

Subsequent files use the same Opportunity folder
Given an Opportunity folder has already been found or created
When additional Timeline Note attachments are created for that same Opportunity
Then those files are copied into the same Opportunity SharePoint folder

Original Note attachment remains intact
Given a Timeline Note attachment is copied to SharePoint
When the automation completes
Then the original attachment is still available on the Timeline Note in Dynamics

Duplicate handling is controlled
Given a file with the same name already exists in the Opportunity SharePoint folder
When another attachment with the same filename is processed
Then the system applies the agreed duplicate handling rule
And does not silently fail

Errors are traceable
Given a file cannot be copied because of missing permissions, invalid path, or SharePoint failure
When the automation runs
Then the failure is visible in flow run history
And, if tracking fields are implemented, the Note is marked with an error status/message

In Scope

Opportunity records only

Timeline Note attachments only

Copy attachment file only

Create missing Opportunity SharePoint folder if needed

Create missing SharePoint Document Location if needed

Make copied files visible in Opportunity Documents tab

Out of Scope

Other Dynamics tables

Copying Note text

Historical backfill of old Notes

SharePoint-to-Dynamics sync

Deleting SharePoint files when Notes are deleted

